Z||000000||fiero56||03-17-2001||10:59 PM||||'88 v-6<P>I just had my injectors rebuilt to eliminate a few fuel related problems. All problems were fixed, except for the fact that my engine still floods from left-over fuel pressure once it is turned off for 30 minutes or more. My only theory on this is that my cold start valve is leaking the fuel, since the injectors are now eliminated as possible culprits. <P>I've never heard of anyone ever having this problem before, just wondering is this is even possible. I checked my local parts places, no-one carries, or can even order it. Seems odd, when you consider how many 2.8s produced with EFI. <P>Carparts does list it, but they have had errors on their site before. gmpartsdirect doesn't carry it. <P>Just wondering if this is a likely source for the fuel leak. Depending how ambitious I feel tommorrow, I might pull it and see if it leaks under pressure.||||reg||5
