Z||000004||Alex4mula||03-19-2001||07:49 AM||||I would try to take the cold start injector out, put fuel presure in the system (without starting obviously) and see if it is realy leaking. I did that once but with the fuel rail to check leaking injectors.<BR>What is the sypmtom? Hard starts warm or cold?||||reg||1
Z||000005||ka4nkf||03-19-2001||04:02 PM||||I had this problem and I finaly found the problem. My fuel punp kept running after I shut it off. The problem was a bad oil sending unit. Listen real close and see if you can hear the fuel pump running after you shut it off. I don't think it would be your cold start switch as it only operates when the star is engaged. If your pump is running after shutdown then unplug the oil pressure switch and see if it stops, If it does then you have found your problem.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ka4nkf||03-19-2001||04:12 PM||||That word in my line about cold start switch ,unstead of star that should be starter.||||reg||1
Z||000007||N_Man||03-19-2001||05:01 PM||||Fiero56, how is your fuel pump?<P>reason i ask is ever since i got my GT it has started like it was flooded, OK leaky injectors expensive to fix so ill live with it.<P>The car does start fine if it has been sitting for more than 24 hours, i assumed that the fuel had time to evaporate from the cylinders.<P>BUT this weekend i hadnt driven the car at all, but had to move it last night, starts right up no suprise... about 10 minutes later i moved it back, starts right up BIG suprise the car never starts right up if it has just run and is off for 10 min.  Then this morning starts right up??? if the injectors were leaky im sure they would have flooded the enginge after i moved the car.<P>So now im left curious of the fuel pump.||||reg||1
Z||000008||skitime||03-19-2001||05:17 PM||||I just checked Autozone again. And they have it for 59.99.  I have learned that even though the local store cannot get the part, if you order it online you will have it in two days.  Order it online.  I tried to get 88 upper A-arm bushing at the local store for 5.99 each. They told me it was a discontinued item and they cannot get it.  I went home and order it online for 4.99 each and had them in two days. Try it.||||reg||1
Z||000009||fiero56||03-19-2001||06:20 PM||||I'll probably get it online. carparts has it for something like $40. I'll pull it just to make sure first, but I'm pretty sure this is the only thing left. <P>Ka4nkf:<P>The fuel pump stops running when I shut the engine off. My problem is that the fuel system "leaks down" the pressure that the fuel pump leaves pressurized once it is shut off. The fuel that "leaks down", leaks into my cylinders. Making for longer cranking times, rough idle until the cylinders clear, and lots of unburnt fuel smell until everything clears out. Plus, its not good for the O2 sensor or the crankcase oil. Technically, you should be able to cycle the f/p on and off an infinite number of times, and never have to fear about the engine flooding with fuel.<P>N-man:<BR>As far as I know, the fuel pump is original, I'd have to go through receipts from previous owner to know for sure. I did check presuure from it few months ago, just killing time playing with my new gage. It was fine as I remember. The longer cranking time have been getting longer and longer over about the last 12 months, now up around 4 seconds, and I can't take it anymore. Now, even in the morning it takes several seconds to fire up. It used to fire instantly when had been sitting for 5 hours or more. Now it does it everytime.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 03-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||88formula||03-19-2001||10:05 PM||||How do you know it’s flooded? <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||skitime||03-20-2001||08:55 AM||||Fiero 56 - Please let me know how replacing the cold start turns out. I have one car doing the same thing. Sometimes it starts hard and sometimes easy. When it starts hard it stumbles a while like its flooded. The factory manual says that to clear a flooded situation to hold athe accelerator to the floor. This tells the computer to reduce fuel.  When it starts hard this tends to help starting which is perhaps a clue.  This car seem to have no rhyme or reason to when it does this. Sometimes hot, sometimes cold, sometimes after sitting long, sometimes after sitting a short while but runs good after it clears.    ||||reg||1
Z||000012||fiero56||03-20-2001||11:54 AM||||88formula:<P>I don't know "for sure" that the engine is flooded. But all the symptoms I see all point to excess fuel in the cylinders.<P>I'll look into the cold start valve soon. I'm not going to be able to order a new one for a little bit. I have to pay for another quarter at school this week, and this is bills week, I'm broke <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Carrolles||03-20-2001||03:59 PM||||Take a look at the fuel injector o-rings.  I got a new set at PepBoys for 50 cents each.  Could be that the fuel rail is bleeding down into the intake after engine stop through a bad o-ring.||||reg||1
